A||||4||jch82||Got My Roof Off........Finally!||||12||
Z||000000||jch82||04-14-2001||02:57 AM||||Well, I went to the junkyard today with Ken and we tried and tried for at least 2hrs to get the stupid roof off of one of the fiero's (it has a sunroof and mine doesn't). Anyways, still haven't got the stupid thing off....One of the bolts stripped out!!@#$@! I still don't know what I'm going to do.  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/frown.gif"> Probably going to have to cut the bolt....<P>After I got home, I ended up taking my roof off. It was the easiest thing I have ever done! I was doing it all wrong at the junkyard (using screwdrivers and what not). All I did was take a sharp knife and run it underneath the A arms to cut through the sealer. <P>At least I know how to get the other one off now.....Guess I can't complain to much since I'm basically getting the roof and sunroof assembly w/ glass for pretty much free....<P>If anyone wants/needs a roof (no sunroof hole), I have one now. It's off an 85GT and its silver. Not sure what they are worth so make me an offer and we can go from there.....<P>BTW, looking for a spoiler so if anyone wants to do some trading....<P>Josh  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/forum/biggrin.gif"><P>------------------<BR>Yeah, my girlfriend takes collect calls from the road<BR>And it doesn't seem to matter that I'm lacking in the bulge<BR>She laughs at my dumb jokes when no one does<BR>She brings me mexican food from Sombrero's just because<BR>                 <I>-Blink 182</I>||||reg||12
Z||000001||FieroJoe||04-14-2001||11:51 PM||||Cool man.  The next Fiero I get will either have a sunroof or I will definatly swap one into it!<P>Kinda late to do it to my coupe, got painted tonight!  (getting excited to put it back together!)<P>------------------<BR>AIM: Snowboarder0311<BR>87 Coupe 5sp. - big resto in progress<BR>  <IMG SRC="http://www.fiero.nl/uploads/profile_1.JPG"> ||||reg||1
Z||000002||mshill||04-15-2001||12:09 AM||||I feel your pain.  I spent 2 hours yesterday getting one off at a pick-n-pull to have it break in two places down below the window area (by the wipers).  All that and the stupid place decided they wanted $70 for it (they only charge $40 for complete hoods). Anyway I bagged it and went to another yard this morning and spent only 30 minutes taking one off and they only wanted $15 for it.  In all I had a decent day at the junkyard.||||reg||1
